<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bas-Rhin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bas-Rhin is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> covering northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, with Strasbourg as its prefecture. Created in 1790, it was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1871 to 1918 and again in practice during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Since 2021 it has formed part of the European Collectivity of Alsace together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haut-rhin">Haut-Rhin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bas-rhin.jpg" alt="Bas-Rhin" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ji-Elle · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strasbourg-Pr%C3%A9fecture.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
